WEBVTT

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.050
Back in 1835, Samuel
Colt made a special gun.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.200
They say this gun can kill anything.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.500
The Colt is gone, and it
seems pretty damn likely

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.100
That the demon is behind all of this.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.200
Whoops.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.100
Crossroads are where pacts are made.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.800
In selling your soul, rituals like this,

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:57.500
You got to put your own
photo into the mix, right?

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.000
I know all about you, Dean Winchester.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:03.100
I'm looking for the best and brightest.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.500
I'm Sam. I'm Jake.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.200
This is a competition.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.300
Only one of you crazy kids

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.000
Is gonna make it out of here alive.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.100
Unh!

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.900
You're tough, you're
smart, you're well-Trained.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.650
Sam, you're my favorite.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:20.300
Sam! Dean!

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:21.600
Sam, look out!

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:23.100
Unh!

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.300
No!

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.500
Sam!!

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:57.800
Dean?

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.400
Brought you this back.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.400
No, thanks. I'm fine.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:12.700
You should eat something.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.300
I said I'm fine.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:27.400
Dean...

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:30.500
I hate to bring this up. I really do.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.100
But don't you think maybe it's time...

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.300
We bury Sam?

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.000
No.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.550
We could maybe...

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.600
What -- Torch
his corpse?

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:50.500
Not yet.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.500
I want you to come with me.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.500
I'm not going anywhere.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:00.000
Dean, please.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:01.700
Won't you cut me some slack?

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.700
I just don't think you
should be alone, that's all.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.500
I got to admit -- I
could use your help.

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:11.500
Something big
is going down --

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.100
End-Of-The-World
big.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:15.450
Well, then let it end!

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.600
You don't mean that.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.400
You don't think so?

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:24.200
Huh?

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.200
You don't think I've given enough?

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.700
You don't think I've paid enough?

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:32.400
I'm done with it.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:34.900
All of it.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.500
And if you know what's good for you,

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:40.200
Turn around and get
the hell out of here.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:44.500
Go!!

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.100
I'm sorry.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:03:59.700
I'm sorry.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:01.900
Please just go.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:13.500
You know where I'll be.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.000
Howdy, Jake.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:58.100
I'm -- I'm
dreaming, aren't I?

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:01.700
I got a genius on my hands.

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:05.700
Well, congratulations, Jake.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.700
You're it --
Last man standing.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:09.900
The american idol.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:11.200
I have to
admit --

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:13.400
You weren't the horse I was betting on,

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:16.200
But still, I got to give it to you.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.700
Go... to hell.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:21.800
Been there, done that.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.600
Everything you
put me through --

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.600
Dragging me to that place,

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.200
Making me kill those people...

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.200
All part of the beauty pageant.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:33.400
Jake, I needed the
strongest, and that's you.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.000
Needed me for what?

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:38.000
Oh, I got a laundry list
of tasty things for you.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.000
The only thing I'm gonna do

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:42.900
Is wake up, hunt you down,

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.800
And kill you myself.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.800
You know, others have tried.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.200
It's not easy.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:54.300
Trust me, Jake. You want to
be a good little soldier here.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:55.800
And if I'm not?

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.100
If you're a bad little soldier,

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:01.300
Well, that dear old mom of yours,

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:04.600
That adorable little sister...

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:09.000
I'll make certain that
they both live long enough

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.300
To know the chewy taste

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.800
Of their own intestines.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.300
No, Jake.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:19.600
I'm not bluffing.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:27.900
What do you want me to do?

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:30.600
Like I said
-- Genius.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:44.600
You know, when
we were little --

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:48.200
You couldn't have
been more than 5 --

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.100
You just started asking questions.

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:57.700
How come we didn't have a mom?

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.100
Why do we always have to move around?

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:03.300
Where'd dad go

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:06.400
When he'd take off for days at a time?

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:10.000
I remember I begged you
-- "Quit asking, Sammy.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.400
Man, you don't want to know."

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.000
I just wanted you to be a kid...

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:20.000
Just for a little while longer.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:25.900
I always tried to protect you

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:30.600
Keep you safe.

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:37.100
Dad didn't even have to tell me.

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:41.900
It was just always my
responsibility, you know?

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:46.800
It's like I had one job...

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:49.900
I had one job...

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:53.500
And I screwed it up.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:00.200
I blew it.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:05.100
And for that, I'm sorry.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.500
I guess that's what I do.

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:18.100
I let down the people I love.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:21.600
I let dad down.

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:28.900
And now I guess I'm just
supposed to let you down, too.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:34.800
How can I?

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:38.900
How am I supposed to live with that?

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:43.000
What am I supposed to do?

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:45.500
Sammy.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:49.800
God.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.700
What am I supposed to do?

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:05.300
What am I supposed to do?!

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.100
Come on, already.

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:14.300
Show your face, you bitch!

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:18.400
Easy, sugar. You'll wake the neighbors.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:26.900
Dean.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:30.500
It is so, so good to see you.

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.900
I mean it. Look at you.

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:38.900
Gone and got your family
killed, all alone in the world.

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:41.300
It's too sweet.

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:46.500
Excuse me. You're gonna
have to give me a moment.

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:48.900
Sometimes you got to
stop and smell the roses.

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:51.400
I should send you straight back to hell.

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:52.900
Oh, you should.

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:54.500
But you won't.

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:58.300
And I know why.

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:01.200
Oh, yeah? Yeah.

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:04.300
Following in daddy's footsteps,
you want to make a deal.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:07.800
Little Sammy back
from the dead, and --

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:10.100
Let me guess, you're
offering up your own soul?

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:12.900
There are a hundred other demons
who'd love to get their hands on it.

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:15.000
And it's all yours.

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:16.800
All you got to do is bring Sam back.

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:18.300
Give me 10 years.

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:21.300
10 years, and then you come for me.

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:22.600
You must be joking.

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:26.100
That's the same deal.You
give everybody else.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:27.800
You're not everybody else.

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:34.300
Why would I want to give you anything?

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:38.500
Just keep your gutter soul.
It's too tarnished, anyways.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:41.600
Nine years.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:42.400
No.

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:45.100
Eight.

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:47.600
You keep going, I'll keep saying no.

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.000
Okay, five years.

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:54.300
Five years, and my bill comes due.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:56.700
That's my last offer --
Five years or no deal.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:05.200
Then no deal.

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:10.200
Fine. Fine

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:15.800
Make sure you bury Sam before
he starts stinking up the joint.

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:18.500
Wait.

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:22.400
It's a fire sale, and
everything must go.

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:27.800
What do I have to do?

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:30.700
First of all, quit groveling.

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:32.600
Needy guys are such a turnoff.

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:37.400
Look...

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:41.600
I shouldn't be doing this. I
could get in a lot of trouble.

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:44.300
But what can I say? I got
a blind spot for you, Dean.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:49.000
You're like a...puppy. You're
just too fun to play with.

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:53.300
I'll do it.

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:54.800
You'll bring him back?

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:55.900
I will.

00:12:57.200 --> 00:12:58.500
And because I'm such a saint,

00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:01.800
I'll give you one
year and one year only.

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:06.000
But here's the thing.

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:10.800
If you try and welch or weasel
your way out, then the deal is off.

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:13.700
Sam drops dead. He's back
to rotten meat in no time.

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:16.900
So...

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:20.300
Its a better deal
than your dad ever got.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:23.900
What do you say?

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:07.400
Sammy.

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:09.300
Thank god

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:10.200
Hey.

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:16.600
Ow.

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:17.700
Uh, Dean...

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:20.000
I'm sorry. I'm sorry, man.

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:21.100
I'm just...

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:23.300
I'm just happy to see you
up and around, that's all.

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:27.000
Come on. Sit down. Okay.

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:30.200
Dean... what happened to me?

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:32.800
Well, what do you remember?

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:35.800
I-I saw you and Bobby, and...

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:39.900
I felt this pain,
this sharp pain like...

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.800
Like, white-Hot, you know, and...

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:44.100
Then you started running at me, and...

00:14:44.600 --> 00:14:45.600
That's about it.

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:48.700
Yeah, that -- That kid
stabbed you in the back.

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:52.900
You lost a lot of blood. It
was touch and go for a while.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:55.400
But, Dean, you -- You can't
patch up a wound that bad.

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:57.500
No, Bobby could.

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:00.900
Who was that kid,anyway?

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:02.500
His name's Jake. Did you get him?

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:04.200
No, he disappeared into the woods.

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:05.700
We got to find him, Dean.

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:08.300
And I swear I'm gonna tear
that son of a bitch apart.

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:10.400
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Easy, van damme.

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:12.600
You just woke up,all right?

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:14.800
Let's get you something to
eat. You want something to eat?

00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:17.300
I'm starving. Come on.

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:19.100
And that's when you guys showed up.

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:21.000
That's awful.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:22.900
Poor Andy.

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:27.200
The demon said he only wanted
one of us to walk out alive.

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:29.000
He told you that? Yep.

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:31.600
He appeared in a dream.

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:33.000
He tell you anything else?

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:36.600
No. No.

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:38.300
That was it. Nothing else.

00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:40.800
You know, what I don't get, Dean,

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:42.700
Is if the demon only wanted one of us,

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:44.500
Then how did Jake and I both get away?

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:47.300
Well, I mean, they left you for dead.

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:48.800
I'm sure they thought it was over.

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:55.200
Now that yellow eyes has Jake,
what's he gonna do with him?

00:15:57.400 --> 00:15:58.400
I don't know.

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:01.100
But whatever it is, we got to stop him.

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:04.100
Hold on, all right? You
need to get your rest.

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:05.100
We got time.

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:06.100
No, we don't.

00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:08.100
Sam, oceans aren't boiling, okay?

00:16:08.200 --> 00:16:09.600
Frogs aren't raining from the sky.

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:11.500
Let's get you your strength back first.

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:15.700
Did you call the Roadhouse?
Do they know anything?

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:17.100
Yeah.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:21.900
Dean...what is it?

00:16:27.100 --> 00:16:29.100
The Roadhouse burned to the ground.
Ash is dead, probably Ellen --

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:30.400
A lot of other hunters, too.

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:34.200
Demons?

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:35.400
Yeah, we think so.

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:37.700
We think because ash found something.

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:38.800
What'd he find?

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:40.800
Bobby's working on that right now.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.400
Well, come on, then. Bobby's
only a few hours away.

00:16:43.700 --> 00:16:46.200
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Stop.
Sam, stop, damn it.

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:51.400
You almost died in there.
I mean, what would I have --

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:56.100
You just take care of
yourself for a little bit, huh?

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:57.300
Just for a little bit.

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:00.200
I'm sorry. No.

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:19.000
Hey, Bobby. Hey, Bobby.

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:21.400
See you up and around.

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:22.900
Yeah, well...

00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:25.100
Thanks for patching me up.

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:27.100
Don't mention it.

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:34.300
Well, Sam's better.

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:36.500
And we're back in it now, so...

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:38.400
What do you know?

00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:46.000
Well, I found something,but...

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:48.600
I'm not sure what the hell it means.

00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:51.000
What is it?

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:55.600
Demonic omens...like a frickin' tidal
wave. Cattle deaths,lightning storms.

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:57.400
They skyrocketed from out of nowhere.

00:17:57.500 --> 00:17:58.400
Here.

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:03.800
All around here
except for one place --

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:05.800
Southern wyoming.

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:06.800
Wyoming?

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:07.500
Yeah.

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:10.200
That one area's totally
clean -- Spotless.

00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:11.900
It's almost as if...

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:12.900
What?

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:15.100
...the demons are surrounding it.

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:16.700
But you don't know why?

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:19.300
No, and by this point,
my eyes are swimming.

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:21.600
Sam, would you take a look at it?

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:23.550
Maybe you can catch
something I couldn't.

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:24.700
Yeah, sure.

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:27.800
Come on, Dean.

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:30.200
I got some more books in the truck.

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:31.800
Help me lug them in.

00:18:34.900 --> 00:18:35.600
Yeah.

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:44.700
You stupid ass! What did you do?

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:47.000
What did you do?!

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:52.100
You made a deal... for Sam, didn't you?

00:18:53.600 --> 00:18:54.700
How long did they give you?

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:55.600
Bobby.

00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:56.900
How long?!

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:02.200
One year.

00:19:02.900 --> 00:19:04.600
Damn it, Dean.

00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:08.000
Which is why we got to find
this yellow-Eyed son of a bitch.

00:19:09.400 --> 00:19:12.700
That's why I'm gonna kill him myself.
I got nothing to lose now,right?

00:19:13.300 --> 00:19:15.200
I could throttle you!

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:17.400
And send me downstairsahead of schedule?

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:24.600
What is it with you Winchesters, huh?

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:26.200
You, your dad,

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:29.700
You're both just itching to
throw yourselves down the pit.

00:19:29.900 --> 00:19:30.800
That's my point.

00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:34.450
Dad brought me back, Bobby. I'm
not even supposed to be here.

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:38.600
At least this way,something good
could come out of it, you know?

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:39.900
It's like my life can mean something.

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:42.400
What? And it didn't before?

00:19:42.900 --> 00:19:45.300
Have you got that low
an opinion of yourself?

00:19:45.400 --> 00:19:47.200
Are you that screwed in the head?!

00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:52.900
I couldn't let him die, Bobby.

00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:55.500
I couldn't.

00:19:56.900 --> 00:19:58.000
He's my brother.

00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:01.900
How is your brother gonna feel

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:04.300
When he knows you're going to hell?

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:09.100
How'd you feel when you
knew your dad went for you?

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:11.800
You can't tell him.

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:14.400
You take a shot at me,
whatever you got to do,

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:15.800
But please don't tell him.

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:37.800
Ellen?

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:40.000
Ellen. Oh, god.

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:53.500
Bobby, is this really necessary?

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:56.400
Just a belt of holy
water. Shouldn't hurt.

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:05.000
Whiskey now, if you don't mind.

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:09.900
Ellen, what happened? How'd you get out?

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:11.200
I wasn't supposed to.

00:21:11.300 --> 00:21:13.200
I was supposed to be in
there with everybody else.

00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:17.600
But we ran out of
pretzels, of all things.

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:19.800
It was just dumb luck.

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:28.600
Anyway, that's when ash
called, panic in his voice.

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:31.300
He told me to look in the safe.

00:21:31.700 --> 00:21:32.700
Then the call cut out.

00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:36.200
By the time I got back,
the flames were sky-High,

00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:38.300
And everybody was dead.

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:40.600
I could n't have been
gone more than 15 minutes.

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:43.300
Sorry, Ellen.

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:45.700
A lot of good people died in there.

00:21:46.900 --> 00:21:48.200
And I got to live.

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:50.900
Lucky me.

00:21:54.100 --> 00:21:55.800
Ellen,you mentioned a safe.

00:21:55.900 --> 00:21:57.300
A hidden safe we keep in the basement.

00:21:57.400 --> 00:21:59.000
Demons get what was in it?

00:21:59.200 --> 00:21:59.800
No.

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:09.600
Wyoming.

00:22:10.200 --> 00:22:11.000
What does that mean?

00:22:14.900 --> 00:22:15.900
I don't believe it.

00:22:18.600 --> 00:22:19.600
What? You got something?

00:22:20.100 --> 00:22:21.300
A lot more than that.

00:22:23.200 --> 00:22:26.600
Each of these x's is an
abandoned frontier church --

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:28.600
All mid-19th century

00:22:28.800 --> 00:22:31.500
And all of them built by Samuel Colt.

00:22:31.600 --> 00:22:34.600
Samuel Colt --The demon-Killing,
gunmaking Samuel Colt?

00:22:34.800 --> 00:22:36.900
Yep. And there's more.

00:22:37.400 --> 00:22:39.600
He built private railway lines

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:41.800
Connecting church to church.

00:22:42.400 --> 00:22:46.200
It just happens to lay out like this.

00:22:47.700 --> 00:22:49.400
Tell me that's not what I think it is.

00:22:49.500 --> 00:22:50.900
It's a devil's trap.

00:22:52.100 --> 00:22:54.200
A 100-Square-Mile
devil's trap.

00:22:54.300 --> 00:22:57.600
That's brilliant. Iron
lines demons can't cross.

00:22:57.700 --> 00:22:59.100
I never heard of anything that massive.

00:22:59.200 --> 00:23:00.200
No one has.

00:23:00.300 --> 00:23:03.200
After all these years none of the
lines are broken? It still works?

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:05.200
Definitely.

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:07.000
How do you know?

00:23:07.100 --> 00:23:08.800
All those omens Bobby found.

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:11.000
That means the demons, they must
be circling and they can't get in.

00:23:11.100 --> 00:23:13.500
Yeah, well... they're trying.

00:23:13.700 --> 00:23:14.800
Why? What's inside?

00:23:15.300 --> 00:23:16.400
That's what I've been looking for,

00:23:16.500 --> 00:23:20.500
And, uh, there's nothing except an old
cowboy cemetery right in the middle.

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:24.100
Well, what's so important
about a cemetery or...

00:23:24.300 --> 00:23:25.700
What's Colt trying to protect?

00:23:26.900 --> 00:23:28.000
Well, unless...

00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:29.200
Unless what?

00:23:30.300 --> 00:23:32.100
What if Colt wasn't trying
to keep the demons out?

00:23:32.200 --> 00:23:33.900
What if he was trying
to keep something in?

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:36.600
That's a comforting
thought. Yeah, you think?

00:23:36.700 --> 00:23:38.400
Could they do it, Bobby?
Could they get inside?

00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:39.500
This thing's so powerful,

00:23:39.600 --> 00:23:42.300
You'd practically need
an a-Bomb to destroy it.

00:23:42.400 --> 00:23:44.400
No way a full-Blood demon gets across.

00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:47.800
No.

00:23:49.400 --> 00:23:50.600
But I know who could.

00:24:22.600 --> 00:24:23.500
Howdy, Jake.

00:24:26.600 --> 00:24:27.900
So, did you have a nice trip?

00:24:28.100 --> 00:24:29.000
I'm here.

00:24:29.200 --> 00:24:31.100
I did what you asked. Now what?

00:24:31.700 --> 00:24:35.100
50 miles thataway, there's
a cemetery, a crypt.

00:24:35.200 --> 00:24:36.600
You got to open that for me.

00:24:37.000 --> 00:24:38.500
Think you can manage that, sport?

00:24:38.700 --> 00:24:40.800
You know what? Screw you
and your freaky orders.

00:24:40.900 --> 00:24:41.800
Go do it yourself.

00:24:41.900 --> 00:24:44.800
Oh, I can't. I can't
go that way -- Not yet.

00:24:44.900 --> 00:24:45.900
Why not?

00:24:48.400 --> 00:24:50.000
I just can't.

00:24:50.400 --> 00:24:53.800
But if you're gonna open that crypt
for me, you're gonna need a key.

00:24:54.300 --> 00:24:55.200
A gun?

00:24:55.300 --> 00:24:57.600
Oh, this isn't just any gun, Jake.

00:24:57.800 --> 00:25:00.800
This is the only gun
in the whole universe

00:25:00.900 --> 00:25:02.800
That can shoot me dead.

00:25:03.900 --> 00:25:05.300
Is that so? Yep.

00:25:05.800 --> 00:25:06.900
Here, take it.

00:25:12.800 --> 00:25:13.700
Oh, my.

00:25:13.900 --> 00:25:17.000
I'm shocked at this
unforeseen turn of events.

00:25:17.100 --> 00:25:19.800
Go ahead, Jake.Squeeze that
trigger. Be all you can be.

00:25:19.900 --> 00:25:22.200
This will all be over. Your
life can go back to normal.

00:25:22.700 --> 00:25:24.800
Of course, the army won't take
you back 'cause you're awol.

00:25:24.900 --> 00:25:28.400
But I'm sure you could get your
old job at the factory back.

00:25:29.500 --> 00:25:30.700
But then, on the other hand,

00:25:30.800 --> 00:25:33.700
The rest of your life and your family's

00:25:33.800 --> 00:25:36.700
Could be money and
honey, health and wealth,

00:25:36.800 --> 00:25:39.000
Every day is ice-Cream sundae.

00:25:39.100 --> 00:25:41.100
And all you got to do
is this one little thing.

00:25:41.200 --> 00:25:42.100
Why me?

00:25:42.200 --> 00:25:45.300
Oh, Jake. It's got to be you.

00:25:45.700 --> 00:25:48.900
I've been waiting for
you for a very long time.

00:25:49.200 --> 00:25:50.100
You're my leader.

00:25:50.200 --> 00:25:52.900
You open that crypt, and
you will have your army.

00:25:53.000 --> 00:25:54.700
You're talking about
the end of the world.

00:25:54.800 --> 00:25:57.400
No, not the end
-- The beginning...

00:25:57.800 --> 00:26:00.600
A better world where your
family will be protected.

00:26:00.700 --> 00:26:02.000
More than that.

00:26:02.900 --> 00:26:04.200
They'll be royalty.

00:26:06.300 --> 00:26:08.100
Buddy boy,you have the chance

00:26:08.200 --> 00:26:11.100
To get in on the ground floor
of a thrilling opportunity.

00:26:11.200 --> 00:26:12.300
What do you say?

00:26:12.500 --> 00:26:13.500
It's your call.

00:26:25.800 --> 00:26:26.900
Attababy.

00:26:53.500 --> 00:26:54.500
Howdy, Jake.

00:27:06.000 --> 00:27:07.000
Wait...

00:27:07.500 --> 00:27:09.700
You were dead.I killed you. Yeah?

00:27:10.600 --> 00:27:11.900
Well, next time, finish the job.

00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:13.100
I did.

00:27:14.000 --> 00:27:16.300
I cut clean through
your spinal cord, man.

00:27:20.500 --> 00:27:22.100
You can't be alive.

00:27:24.200 --> 00:27:25.300
You can't be.

00:27:25.600 --> 00:27:28.500
Okay, just take it real easy there, son.

00:27:28.900 --> 00:27:29.900
And if I don't?

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:31.200
Wait and see.

00:27:32.800 --> 00:27:34.500
What, you a tough guy all of a sudden?

00:27:35.200 --> 00:27:36.800
What are you gonna
do -- Kill me?

00:27:37.000 --> 00:27:37.900
It's a thought.

00:27:38.000 --> 00:27:40.000
You had your chance. You couldn't.

00:27:40.300 --> 00:27:42.000
I won't make that mistake twice.

00:27:46.600 --> 00:27:48.400
What are you smiling
at, you little bitch?

00:27:51.100 --> 00:27:52.000
Hey, lady.

00:27:53.700 --> 00:27:54.700
Do me a favor.

00:27:56.300 --> 00:27:57.900
Put that gun to your head.

00:28:09.400 --> 00:28:10.700
See, that ava girl was right.

00:28:10.800 --> 00:28:11.700
Once you give in to it,

00:28:11.800 --> 00:28:14.700
There's all sorts of new jedi
mind tricks you can learn.

00:28:14.800 --> 00:28:15.800
Let her go.

00:28:16.100 --> 00:28:17.600
Shoot him.

00:28:18.100 --> 00:28:20.100
You'll be mopping up skull
before you get a shot off.

00:28:22.900 --> 00:28:25.200
Everybody, put your guns down.

00:28:27.300 --> 00:28:28.700
Except you, sweetheart.

00:28:47.800 --> 00:28:48.700
Okay.

00:28:49.200 --> 00:28:50.000
Thank you.

00:29:19.800 --> 00:29:22.400
Please...don't.

00:29:23.100 --> 00:29:24.100
Please.

00:29:56.400 --> 00:29:57.200
Oh, no.

00:29:57.500 --> 00:29:58.400
Bobby, what is it?

00:29:59.700 --> 00:30:00.700
It's hell.

00:30:03.400 --> 00:30:04.500
Take cover
-- Now!

00:30:26.300 --> 00:30:27.000
What the hell just happened?!

00:30:27.100 --> 00:30:30.100
That's a devil's gate,
a damn door to hell!

00:30:38.200 --> 00:30:40.000
Come on! We got to shut that gate!

00:30:50.100 --> 00:30:51.600
If the demon gave this to Jake...

00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:53.900
Then maybe...

00:31:01.700 --> 00:31:03.300
A boy shouldn't play with daddy's guns.

00:31:20.100 --> 00:31:21.100
Dean!

00:31:27.700 --> 00:31:29.300
I'll get to you in a minute, champ.

00:31:29.600 --> 00:31:32.000
I'm proud of you --
Knew you had it in you.

00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:40.000
Sit a spell.

00:31:44.800 --> 00:31:46.400
So, Dean...

00:31:46.800 --> 00:31:48.400
I got to thank you.

00:31:48.600 --> 00:31:51.300
You see, demons can't resurrect people

00:31:51.400 --> 00:31:52.700
Unless a deal is made.

00:31:52.800 --> 00:31:55.300
I know, red tape --
It'll make you nuts.

00:31:55.400 --> 00:31:59.100
But thanks to you,
Sammy's back in rotation.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:02.300
Now, I wasn't counting
on that, but I'm glad.

00:32:02.400 --> 00:32:04.400
I liked him better than Jake, anyhow.

00:32:06.200 --> 00:32:07.100
Tell
me --

00:32:07.200 --> 00:32:08.100
Have you ever heard the expression

00:32:08.200 --> 00:32:11.500
"If a deal sounds too good
to be true, it probably is"?

00:32:11.800 --> 00:32:13.500
You call that deal good?

00:32:13.900 --> 00:32:16.200
It's a better shake
than your dad ever got.

00:32:16.700 --> 00:32:19.500
And you never wondered why?

00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:21.400
I'm surprised at you.

00:32:22.200 --> 00:32:23.000
I mean...

00:32:23.800 --> 00:32:26.600
You saw what your brother
just did to Jake, right?

00:32:26.900 --> 00:32:29.000
That was pretty cold,wasn't it?

00:32:32.000 --> 00:32:34.000
How certain are you

00:32:34.100 --> 00:32:38.250
That what you brought
back is 100% pure Sam?

00:32:47.400 --> 00:32:48.899
You of all people should know

00:32:48.900 --> 00:32:51.800
That what's dead should stay dead.

00:32:53.800 --> 00:32:54.600
Anyway...

00:32:56.100 --> 00:32:57.600
Thanks a bunch.

00:32:57.800 --> 00:33:00.300
I knew I kept you alive for some reason.

00:33:00.700 --> 00:33:02.200
Until now, anyway.

00:33:03.900 --> 00:33:05.000
I couldn't have done it

00:33:05.100 --> 00:33:07.200
Without your pathetic, self-Loathing,

00:33:07.300 --> 00:33:09.400
Self-Destructive desire

00:33:09.500 --> 00:33:11.800
To sacrifice yourself for your family.

00:35:56.300 --> 00:35:58.200
Well, check that off the to-Do list.

00:35:59.900 --> 00:36:00.900
You did it.

00:36:01.500 --> 00:36:02.600
I didn't do it alone.

00:36:05.600 --> 00:36:07.000
Do you think dad really...

00:36:08.700 --> 00:36:10.700
Do you think he really
climbed out of hell?

00:36:12.200 --> 00:36:13.600
The door was open.

00:36:17.100 --> 00:36:18.800
If anyone's stubborn enough to do it...

00:36:21.300 --> 00:36:22.300
It would be him.

00:36:27.300 --> 00:36:28.700
Where do you think he is now?

00:36:31.400 --> 00:36:32.400
I don't know.

00:36:35.100 --> 00:36:37.400
I kind of can't believe
it, Dean.I mean...

00:36:39.000 --> 00:36:40.600
Our whole lives,everything...

00:36:41.300 --> 00:36:43.300
Has been prepping for this, and now I...

00:36:47.500 --> 00:36:49.300
I kind of don't know what to say.

00:36:53.100 --> 00:36:53.900
I do.

00:37:03.300 --> 00:37:04.900
That was for our mom...

00:37:07.200 --> 00:37:08.700
You son of a bitch.

00:37:18.400 --> 00:37:19.900
You know, when Jake saw me...

00:37:20.600 --> 00:37:22.000
It was like he saw a ghost.

00:37:26.700 --> 00:37:28.400
I mean, hell, you heard him, Dean.

00:37:29.800 --> 00:37:30.800
He said he killed me.

00:37:33.700 --> 00:37:34.900
I'm glad he was wrong.

00:37:35.300 --> 00:37:36.700
I don't think he was,Dean.

00:37:40.300 --> 00:37:43.000
What happened... after I was stabbed?

00:37:44.900 --> 00:37:46.800
I already told you. Not everything.

00:37:49.200 --> 00:37:51.000
Sam, we just killed the demon.

00:37:53.000 --> 00:37:54.800
Can we celebrate for a minute?

00:38:00.100 --> 00:38:01.300
Did I die?

00:38:01.600 --> 00:38:03.000
Oh, come on.

00:38:03.800 --> 00:38:06.100
Did you sell your soul for
me, like dad did for you?

00:38:06.200 --> 00:38:07.100
Come on! No

00:38:12.300 --> 00:38:13.400
Tell me the truth.

00:38:16.300 --> 00:38:17.600
Dean, tell me the truth.

00:38:17.700 --> 00:38:18.600
Sam...

00:38:29.500 --> 00:38:30.750
How long do you get?

00:38:36.700 --> 00:38:37.700
One year.

00:38:40.300 --> 00:38:41.400
I got one year.

00:38:44.700 --> 00:38:46.000
You shouldn't have done that.

00:38:47.100 --> 00:38:48.100
How could you do that?

00:38:48.200 --> 00:38:49.300
Don't get mad at me.

00:38:51.700 --> 00:38:52.700
Don't you do that.

00:38:55.000 --> 00:38:56.000
I had to.

00:38:57.200 --> 00:38:58.700
I had to look out for you.

00:39:00.100 --> 00:39:01.100
That's my job.

00:39:01.200 --> 00:39:02.900
And what do you think my job is?

00:39:03.400 --> 00:39:04.100
What?

00:39:04.500 --> 00:39:07.700
You saved my life over and over.

00:39:08.300 --> 00:39:09.600
I mean, you sacrifice everything for me.

00:39:09.700 --> 00:39:11.400
Don't you think I'd do the same for you?

00:39:14.600 --> 00:39:15.500
You're my big brother.

00:39:16.600 --> 00:39:19.700
There's nothing I wouldn't do for you.

00:39:23.900 --> 00:39:26.300
And I don't care what it takes.
I'm gonna get you out of this.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:32.100
Guess I got to save
your ass for a change.

00:39:33.900 --> 00:39:34.500
Yeah.

00:39:36.000 --> 00:39:36.800
Well...

00:39:37.900 --> 00:39:39.700
Yellow-Eyed demon might be dead,

00:39:40.000 --> 00:39:41.800
But a lot more got through that gate.

00:39:42.000 --> 00:39:43.000
How many, you think?

00:39:43.600 --> 00:39:46.200
100, maybe 200.

00:39:46.500 --> 00:39:47.500
It's an army.

00:39:49.000 --> 00:39:50.500
He's unleashed an army.

00:39:53.500 --> 00:39:55.100
Hope to hell you boys are ready.

00:39:55.800 --> 00:39:57.400
'Cause the war has just begun.

00:39:59.900 --> 00:40:01.000
Well, then...

00:40:10.700 --> 00:40:12.000
We got work to do.



00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.000
